win32u, winemac: share Vulkan memory through Metal objects on macOS (VK_EXT_external_memory_metal).

Windows programs share textures between Direct3D devices through NT or global handles, which winevulkan exposes as
VK_KHR_external_memory_win32. win32u implemented that only on top of the host's VK_KHR_external_memory_fd: the
exported allocation became an fd kept in a D3DKMT resource, and the importer got the fd back. MoltenVK has no fd
memory, so on macOS the extension was missing: DXVK logged "Failed to create shared resource:
VK_KHR_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_WIN32 not supported" and vkd3d-proton's OpenSharedHandle failed. Media Foundation decodes
video through D3D11 (DXVK) and a D3D12 renderer (vkd3d-proton) opens the frames by handle, so Microsoft Flight
Simulator 2024 showed black where its boot, loading and start screens play videos.

On a host without fd memory but with VK_EXT_external_memory_metal, win32u now exports the allocation as a Metal
object (an MTLTexture for memory dedicated to an image, an MTLBuffer for one dedicated to a buffer, the MTLHeap
otherwise), keeps it in a process-local table keyed by the inode of a pipe, and hands that pipe to the D3DKMT
resource in place of the fd. Opening the resource returns the pipe, the inode finds the object, and the import goes
through VkImportMemoryMetalHandleInfoEXT. The D3DKMT handles, their runtime data (DXVK's and vkd3d-proton's
description of the resource) and the Windows side are unchanged. winemac maps VK_KHR_external_memory_win32 to
VK_EXT_external_memory_metal. Only the process that created a resource can open it: another process would need an
IOSurface. Keyed mutexes and shared fences are not covered (they need semaphore export).

Needs Highball's MoltenVK patch "Keep an imported MTLTexture as the memory of a dedicated image".
Checked on an M4 (macOS 27.0): a test program creating a shared D3D11 texture (NT and global handle), clearing it,
opening it in D3D12 and copying it back reads the cleared color; MSFS 2024 plays its boot and loading videos.

